Falsifies `byte_glob::verification::the_case_fold_ignores_the_case_of_the_name`.

The defect: under the case fold, `class_at` tests only the name's byte and never its other case, so `[a]`
matches `a` but not `A` while a literal `a` matches both.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` of the match on the name and on the lowercased name.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -612,7 +612,7 @@ fn class_at(pattern: &[u8], open: usize, c: u8, case: Case) -> (Option<(bool, us
     // Under a fold, the name's byte is a member when either case of it is. `other` is `c` itself
     // for a byte that is not an ASCII letter, and under `Case::Sensitive`.
     let other = match case {
-        Case::AsciiInsensitive => other_case(c),
+        Case::AsciiInsensitive => c,
         Case::Sensitive => c,
     };
     let mut k = open + 1;
